    "body": "## Summary\n\n`DeepSpeedEngine._get_shared_params()` walks the module tree with\n`named_children()`, which **de-duplicates children by identity**. When an entire\nsubmodule — not just a tied leaf `Parameter` — is aliased under a second\nattribute name, the second name's subtree is never visited. Its parameters are\ntherefore never recorded as shared, and they go missing from the state dict\nreconstructed by `zero_to_fp32.py` / `load_state_dict_from_zero_checkpoint()`\nafter a ZeRO stage 1/2/3 checkpoint.\n\n`nn.Module.state_dict()` itself walks `_modules` directly and does not\nde-duplicate, so the save path and this reconstruction path disagree about which\nnames exist.\n\nFixes #1789\n\n**Impact: silent-wrong-result**\n\nWho reaches it: any model that reuses a whole child module under two attribute\nnames (`self.layer2 = self.layer1`) and is checkpointed with ZeRO. No special\nconfiguration is needed. The failure is silent — the checkpoint is written\nwithout error and the missing keys only surface later, as a `load_state_dict`\nfailure or, worse, as a silently incomplete model.\n\nThe de-duplication is easy to confirm in isolation:\n\n```python\ninner = nn.Linear(2, 2)\nm = nn.Module(); m.a = inner; m.b = inner\n[n for n, _ in m.named_children()]   # ['a']       <- 'b' is dropped\n[n for n, _ in m._modules.items()]   # ['a', 'b']\n```\n\n## Changes\n\n- Walk `module._modules.items()` instead of `named_children()`, matching the\n  traversal `nn.Module.state_dict()` uses.\n- Add `test_get_shared_params_records_aliased_submodule`, which exercises\n  `_get_shared_params()` directly.\n\nA note on that test: this file's existing end-to-end conversion test requires an\naccelerator and is skipped in most environments, so it cannot demonstrate this\ndefect. The bug is in the tree walk, and `_get_shared_params()` reads only\n`self.module`, `zero_optimization_partition_weights()` and the rank — so the\ntraversal can be driven directly, at the level the defect actually lives. The\nend-to-end case is kept for environments that can run it.\n\n## Validation\n\nNegative control — with the change to `engine.py` reverted and the test left in\nplace:\n\n```\nFAILED test_get_shared_params_records_aliased_submodule\n  AssertionError: assert None == 'layer1.weight'\n1 failed in 3.34s\n```\n\nWith the fix, and the rest of the file alongside it:\n\n```\n1 passed in 3.25s\n5 passed, 2 skipped in 3.88s\n```\n\nSigned-off-by: Udaya Tejas <udayatejas2004@gmail.com>\n",
